		{
			dependencies: ["514EC4ADAD6F5535"]
			description: [
				"Now that we have all the resources to build the cannons, let's get started by following the steps:"
				""
				"1- You need to build a 3x3 cannon cast with a gap in the middle using the &6Casting Sand&r, do this for each part of the cannon."
				""
				"2- Now you need to prepare the cannon cast to receive the &6Molten Steel&r, to do this you need to use a &6Cast Mould&r that is compatible for each type of &6Cannon Layer&r, then right click with &6Cast Mould&r in the right hand on the gap to make the sand mould. Right click again to take the &6Cast Mould&r back."
				""
				"3- Then you need to fill the gap with &6Molten Steel&r, after this you need to wait a little for the cannon part cool down. You can use both &6Molten Steel&r from Tinkers or Big Cannons."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"  Tip: Cannon casts can output redstone signal that can be read by &6Comparator&r, they output a redstone signal from 0 to 14 to show how full it is, when reach 15 it's ready ( put a &6Nixie Tube&r next to the comparator to see the numbers ). If you need a visual explanation hold \"W\" on the &6Casting Sand&r to see the ponder."
				""
				"4- Now that we have the &6Unbored Cannon Layer&r just take it back the &6Casting Sand&r, to do this quickly just right click with your empty hand."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "createbigcannons:autocannon_ammo_container"
				tag: { }
			}
			id: "4C7826C8A5521396"
			tasks: [{
				id: "046F9FFA9F2094BF"
				title: "Automated"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Cannon Casting 101"
			x: 4.5d
			y: -0.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"4F89EA707FA4EB2D"
				"43E53DAA34175B35"
				"181284F9FCDF0979"
			]
			icon: "createbigcannons:cannon_builder"
			id: "084D5FBCD0FAA13C"
			tasks: [
				{
					consume_items: false
					id: "4D9F531A7FF98562"
					item: "createbigcannons:cannon_builder"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					count: 5L
					id: "04F2F7A100B82D9D"
					item: { Count: 5, id: "create:piston_extension_pole" }
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "19E89C851715C20B"
