		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"61072A036F885AB9"
				"130A48A22011EE9E"
				"5C09C6DC2C2D8D90"
			]
			description: [
				"1- Then we'll transform the &6Unbored Cannon Layer&r in just a &6Cannon Layer&r, now you need to setup a &6Cannon Drill&r and a &6Mechanical Bearing&r to make this happen."
				""
				"  Tip: Hold \"W\" on the &6Cannon Drill&r ( The ponder show you exactly how you can make this process ) or press \"U\" in any &6Cannon Layer&r, now you have an idea of how you can setup these machines to work."
				""
				"IMPORTANT- You noticed that over the process of drilling the \"Unbored Cannon Layer\" they drop scraps of the material. These scraps you can throw them in a &6Basin&r + &6Basin Foundry Lid&r, heat them up to get a part of your steel back."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"2- Repeat the steps 1, 2, 3 and 4 from the previous quest and the first of this one for each type of &6Cannon Layer&r that we're asking for, they are needed to get our &6Cannon Chamber&r because it's from him we get the &6Steel Ring&r. Now you have the very small, small and medium &6Unbored Cannon Layer&r, we'll use them to built up our &6Cannon Chamber&r."
				""
				"3- To build our &6Cannon Chamber&r we need a &6Cannon Builder&r with some &6Extension Piston Pole&r. The &6Cannon Builder&r needs redstone signal to work, when the redstone signal is active the &6Cannon Builder&r will glue the &6Cannon Layer&r in him, then ou can add rotation power to bring together the &6Cannon Layer&r, once the layers are stack-up turn off the redstone signal and bring back the piston."
				""
				"Tip: If you need a visual explanation of the step 7 you can hold \"W\" on the &6Cannon Builder&r, but notice that they use a different cannon to give you an example."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
